# Story E20260921ad0d45c9:S006 / t4 — the .vsix content boundary.
#
# The extension is BUNDLED (esbuild inlines the thin shared ipc-client), so the
# raw TypeScript source, the tests, the typecheck config, the bundler config,
# and the sibling repo `src/` never need to ship. The .vsix carries ONLY the
# runtime bits + Marketplace listing assets:
#   package.json, out/ (the bundle), assets/ (installer + steering-block),
#   README.md, icon.png, LICENSE
# Everything else is excluded — no source, no tests, no daemon internals (k5).

# TypeScript source + tests (bundled into out/, never shipped raw)
src/**
**/__tests__/**
**/*.test.ts
**/*.ts

# Build / typecheck / bundler config
tsconfig.json
esbuild.mjs

# Repo tooling that is not part of the runtime package
.github/**
.vscode/**
.gitignore
.npmrc

# NOTE: the sibling repo `src/` (the daemon internals) is never at risk of being
# packaged — vsce only ever includes files WITHIN the package root, and the
# esbuild bundle inlined only the thin ipc-client (k5). No glob is needed for it.
